---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ProjectGrid from '../components/ProjectGrid.astro';
import ProjectMedia from '../components/ProjectMedia.astro';
import IntentPicker from '../components/IntentPicker.astro';
import { withBase, inquiryLabel } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout title="Quiet Compass — clearer websites and digital products" description="An independent digital studio exploring clearer websites, stronger identities and simpler product flows. Inspect original concept studies and the decisions behind them." route="A01">
 <nav class="route-rail" aria-label="Page route" data-pagefind-ignore><a data-route-link href="#arrival">Arrival</a><a data-route-link href="#work">Work</a><a data-route-link href="#method">Method</a><a data-route-link href="#thinking">Direction</a><a data-route-link href="#contact">Contact</a></nav>
 <section id="arrival" data-element="earth" data-bearing="35"><div class="hero shell">
  <div><span class="route">Independent digital studio · concept portfolio</span><h1>Complicated,<br/><em>made clear.</em></h1><p class="lead">Clearer websites. Stronger identities. More thoughtful product flows. Explore the decisions—not just the finished screens.</p><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary magnetic" href="#work">See selected work ↗</a><a class="btn magnetic" href={withBase('contact/')}>{inquiryLabel} →</a></div><p class="hero-note">Strategy · Identity · Product design · Web development</p></div>
  <a class="feature-card" href={withBase('projects/atlas/')} aria-label="Explore Atlas, a concept study in workflow design"><div class="feature-meta"><span class="route">Featured route / Atlas</span><span class="pill">Concept study</span></div><ProjectMedia slug="atlas" priority alt="Atlas concept: four navigation groups beside a focused request-review workspace" sizes="(max-width:820px) 92vw, 45vw" transitionName="featured-atlas"/><div class="feature-caption"><div><h2>Less searching.<br/>A clearer next step.</h2><p>See how seven navigation choices become four groups.</p></div><span class="compass" aria-hidden="true"></span></div></a>
 </div></section>
 <div class="evidence-band"><div class="shell"><strong>Three original studies.</strong><span>Real design artifacts. Synthetic examples.</span><span>No invented client results.</span></div></div>
 <section id="work" data-element="water" data-bearing="85"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">B02 / Selected work</span><h2>See what changes.<br/>Understand why.</h2></div><p>From a busy workspace to an onboarding flow: each study shows the starting point, an alternative, and a considered direction. All three are self-initiated concepts.</p></div><ProjectGrid limit={3}/><div class="actions"><a class="text-link" href={withBase('work/')}>Browse by design focus →</a></div></div></section>
 <section id="method" class="method-section" data-element="wood" data-bearing="145"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">C03 / The approach</span><h2>Ask carefully.<br/>Make deliberately.</h2></div><p>A good-looking screen is the beginning of a conversation, not the end of the work. The useful question is what becomes easier for the person using it.</p></div><div class="method-grid"><article class="method-card"><span class="number">01</span><h3>Discover the real decision.</h3><p>Map the task, the people and the constraints. Separate what is known from what still needs to be tested.</p><span class="route">Output / a clear question</span></article><article class="method-card"><span class="number">02</span><h3>Shape a useful answer.</h3><p>Explore alternatives in working artifacts. Keep the tradeoffs visible and the explanation close to the design.</p><span class="route">Output / an inspectable prototype</span></article><article class="method-card"><span class="number">03</span><h3>Deliver, then verify.</h3><p>Build the responsive system, check the complete journey, and test the published experience—not just a mockup.</p><span class="route">Output / a system that holds up</span></article></div></div></section>
 <section id="thinking" data-element="metal" data-bearing="230"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">D04 / Find your direction</span><h2>What needs to<br/>become clearer?</h2></div><p>Choose a starting point. You will get a relevant study and a reason to explore it, right here.</p></div><IntentPicker/></div></section>
 <section data-element="earth"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><span class="route">From the journal</span><h2>A little more<br/>of the thinking.</h2></div><a class="text-link" href={withBase('journal/')}>Read the journal →</a></div><div class="journal-grid"><article class="journal-card"><span class="route">Interaction</span><h3>Calm does not have to mean still.</h3><p>Three ways an interface can feel alive without turning attention into a competition.</p><a class="text-link" href={withBase('journal/calm-interfaces/')} >Read the essay →</a></article><article class="journal-card"><span class="route">Workflow design</span><h3>Start with decisions, not screens.</h3><p>What the Atlas concept reveals when the navigation is treated as a task map.</p><a class="text-link" href={withBase('journal/decisions-not-screens/')} >Read the essay →</a></article><article class="journal-card"><span class="route">Access</span><h3>A quieter mode, equally complete.</h3><p>Why reduced motion deserves a deliberate design—not an empty version of the page.</p><a class="text-link" href={withBase('journal/reduced-motion/')} >Read the essay →</a></article></div></div></section>
 <section id="contact" data-element="fire" data-bearing="320"><div class="shell next-action"><div><span class="route">E05 / The next step</span><h2>Start with what<br/>you need to change.</h2><p class="muted measure">A useful brief begins with the problem, the people and the outcome you have in mind.</p></div><div class="actions"><a class="btn primary magnetic" href={withBase('contact/')}>{inquiryLabel} →</a></div></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
